    preview: "Justifiedâ or no business being thereâ? Tennessee munitions town loyal to Trump but divided on Iran Kingsport, Tennessee, is a manufacturing town in the foothills of the Appalachian Mountains. Home to generations of industrial workers, it is home to an ammunitions plant that manufactures explosives that the US military relies on. It has long been a Republican stronghold and many voters there say they still plan to support the Republican Party, despite concerns about the economy and promises of no more wars.",
    body: "Justifiedâ or no business being thereâ? Tennessee munitions town loyal to Trump but divided on Iran\n\nKingsport, Tennessee, is a manufacturing town in the foothills of the Appalachian Mountains. Home to generations of industrial workers, it is home to an ammunitions plant that manufactures explosives that the US military relies on. It has long been a Republican stronghold and many voters there say they still plan to support the Republican Party, despite concerns about the economy and promises of no more wars. The BBC's Sheila Flynn went to speak to voters in the Bible Belt town.\n\nVideo by Eloise Alanna.\n\nRelated topics\n\n- TennesseeUpdates from your News topics will appear in My News and in a collection on the News homepage.\n\n- IranUpdates from your News topics will appear in My News and in a collection on the News homepage.\n\n- Donald TrumpUpdates from your News topics will appear in My News and in a collection on the News homepage.\n\n- United StatesUpdates from your News topics will appear in My News and in a collection on the News homepage.",
